    54	  nonzerodivisor on R/J globally, hence on A_m. Rees ideal `:24-25`: H = J + (g y_j - G_j y_q), `sat(H,g)`. Over R_g the
    55	  ideal I is principal (g) and the kernel of R_g[y] -> R_g[It] is generated by y_j - (G_j/g) y_q; the Rees kernel is
    56	  g-saturated because g is a nonzerodivisor on R/J and so on R[It] subset (R/J)[T]. So sat(H,g) is the Rees ideal.
