    58	  sum I^d/mI^d, each summand killed by m, so it equals its localization at m: global = local, and no component of
    59	  Rees(I) away from the origin enters. This holds only because the boundary point is the origin of the translated
    60	  coordinates (true by construction of the inputs) and because I is generated by the same G locally and globally.
