     1	# Decision record: the four failed A_5 fiber runs
     2	
     3	Inputs: `purpose.md` (target object), `first-principles-plan.md` (Claude sonnet consultant, "CP"),
     4	`codex-consult-v2.md` (Codex gpt-6.1-sol high, read-only, "CX"). Times UTC. Every step states its falsifier before it
     5	runs; results are appended under each step with log paths.
     6	
     7	## 1. Target
     8	
     9	Proj F(I), F(I) = sum_d I^d / m I^d, for I = (G) the kernel-coordinate ideal on the nullity-8 closure Y at a point of
    10	the boundary orbit Z. Deliverable per pair: dimension, degree, Hilbert series, components. A finite segment h_1..h_d is
    11	partial. CX qualification adopted: I = (G) is the Pfaffian kernel-coordinate ideal; its identification with the ideal
    12	of Z is not assumed, and the fiber of (G) is what the attachment needs (the kernel limit set), so (G) is the right
    13	center. Computations over F_32009 certify that reduction only; characteristic-zero claims need a second prime and a
    14	specialization argument (CX).
    15	
    16	## 2. Reconciliation of the two consultants
    17	
    18	| Point | CP | CX | Decision and reason |
    19	|---|---|---|---|
    20	| Local `ds` syzygy is the cost driver; replace by global membership in J + m P_d ("A") | yes, measured 17 s vs 25,459 s at X- d=2 | yes, same proof (quotient killed by m) | **Adopt.** Two independent derivations; measured. |
    21	| Nakayama normal-monomial reduction (680 -> 122 X, 969 -> 265 Iso) | yes | yes, local justification suffices | **Adopt.** |
    22	| X+ and X- related by t9 -> -t9 with sign vectors on J and G | not seen | checked coefficient-wise | **Adopt after S0 verifies it in Singular.** Halves the X work. |
    23	| Full fiber by pivot saturation H : g^inf, F = k[t,y]/((H:g^inf)+(t)) ("B") | not proposed | proposed, M2 ReesAlgebra uses the same mechanism | **Adopt as the completion certificate.** It is the only route giving the whole ideal, hence the Hilbert series and components without a completeness gap. |
    24	| Regularity of k[y]/K2 bounds missing relations (CP R7) | proposed | refuted: regularity of K2 says nothing about relations of the unknown F(I) | **Reject.** CX is right; a new relation can appear in any degree. |
    25	| Radical first + `minAssChar` for X- V(K2): one prime, degree 12 | measured 1 s | agrees; arithmetic irreducibility over F_p only | **Adopt, with the F_p qualifier.** V(K2) is only an upper bound for the fiber until B or a complete A closes it. |
    26	| msolve on the 31-variable a-graph | "not the tool" | low priority, not refuted universally | **Deprioritize, do not run.** B removes the a-graph entirely; a 64 GiB msolve replay buys a comparison, not the object. |
    27	| Generic linear section / Frobenius orbits for Iso components (CP R4) | proposed | diagnostic only | **Reject as evidence; keep as a sanity check if cheap.** |
    28	| Torus multigrading makes decomposition cheap (CP R5) | proposed | grading splits blocks, does not force toric components | **Defer.** Use only if Iso chart decomposition stalls. |
    29	| Projective-chart decomposition for Iso K2 / fiber | not proposed | proposed | **Adopt for Iso** after B gives the fiber ideal. |
    30	| One-point transport by H-transitivity | assumed | the split boost has no kernel lift (program doc line 23) | **Reject the assumption.** Each pair is computed at its recorded point; no transport claim. |
    31	| Fiber dim bounds | "at most 3" universally | 3 X, 4 Iso and E8-bar, 5 W8 from germ dimensions | **Adopt CX bounds** as falsifiers. |
    32	| W8 product count | 325 | 300 | **300** (24*25/2). |
    33	| Sparse Macaulay linear algebra with upper/lower sandwich | Wiedemann idea | gives a certified stop rule | **Hold in reserve** for a degree where A's std blows up. |
    34	| GPU/TPU rank infrastructure | listed | lowest priority until a matrix problem is measured | **Reject for now.** No measured matrix bottleneck. |
    35	| New packages (Normaliz, 4ti2, CoCoA, OSCAR, msolve master) | not needed | same | **Build none now.** Installed Singular 4.4.1 and Macaulay2 cover A and B. |
    36	| Resource limits | cgroup `MemoryMax`, never `prlimit --as` | same, with `MALLOC_ARENA_MAX=2`, one thread | **Adopt.** Both prior killers (xp_np, msolve solo, probe H) were address-space caps. |
    37	
    38	## 3. Falsification of the whole plan
    39	
    40	The plan fails if any of these holds; each is checked by a step below.
    41	- F1. The sign symmetry fails on any generator: X+ must be computed separately.
    42	- F2. Method A at d=2 does not reproduce h2 = 51 (X) / 85 (Iso): A is wrong or the inputs differ.
    43	- F3. A at d=3 gives h3 > 122 (X) or > 265 (Iso): the Nakayama reduction or the code is wrong.
    44	- F4. B's Hilbert function disagrees with A in any degree A completed: one of the two is wrong; neither result stands.
    45	- F5. B's fiber dimension exceeds the germ bound (3 X, 4 Iso/E8-bar, 5 W8).
    46	- F6. B fails at the chosen pivot because g is a zero divisor mod J: choose another pivot; if none, B is unavailable.
    47	- F7. The fiber is not contained in V(K2) (B's degree-2 part differs from K2): input or code error.
