    33	**Method B also passes.** The colon test establishes \((J:g)=J\), a sufficient global nonzerodivisor condition. The template then forms \(H\), saturates by \(g\), and specializes every source variable to zero ([b_body.sing:5](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/templates/b_body.sing:5), [b_body.sing:11](~/Projects/IBMQuantum/docs/local/a5-failed-runs/templates/b_body.sing:11)). Rees formation commutes with localization at the origin. After specialization, every inverted source polynomial with nonzero constant term becomes an invertible scalar. Components confined away from the origin therefore contribute nothing to this fiber. The installed `sat` returns an ideal, matching the assignment ([elim.lib:717](/usr/share/singular/LIB/elim.lib:717)).
